# Docker
.dockerignore
# Exception: this one is real and load-bearing (excludes swaya-extension/'s
# dev tooling from docker_image.code_server_multi's build context, same
# node_modules-bloat class of problem that broke `coder templates push`
# — see project_coder_submit_extension.md) — the blanket rule above is
# unused boilerplate from the initial project scaffold, not protecting
# against any other real .dockerignore in this repo.
!infra/coder-templates/code-server-multi/.dockerignore

# Frontend
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/build/
frontend/.vite/
frontend/.turbo

# swaya-submit-timer VS Code extension (infra/coder-templates/code-server-multi) —
# node_modules is dev-only tooling (typescript/@types), never needed at
# `coder templates push` time and must NOT be present then (blows past the
# Coder server's 1MB template-archive limit, see
# project_coder_submit_extension.md). out/ is reproducible from src/ via
# `npx tsc` — the committed .vsix (built via `npx vsce package`) is the one
# build artifact that actually needs to be tracked, since main.tf's
# filebase64() reads it directly and nothing in the deploy pipeline rebuilds
# it automatically.
infra/coder-templates/code-server-multi/swaya-extension/node_modules/
infra/coder-templates/code-server-multi/swaya-extension/out/

# Local deploy script (contains server-specific paths — use deploy_template.sh)
deploy.sh

